 To find the LCM of $14$, $20$, and $35$, we first factor each number:
\begin{align*}
14 &= 2 \cdot 7 \\
20 &= 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 5 \\
35 &= 5 \cdot 7
\end{align*}
The LCM of $14$, $20$, and $35$ is the product of the distinct prime factors with the highest powers:
\begin{align*}
2^2 &\cdot 5^1 \cdot 7^1 \\
&= 4 \cdot 5 \cdot 7 \\
&= 140.
\end{align*}

